findings.body:
The auto-increment branch does not check `dev`, so `tauri android dev` (`dev.rs:274`, which passes `true`) increments the stored version code on every invocation. A dev session with a few restarts can push the counter well ahead of what a release needs, and a dev run that fails later in the pipeline still writes the new value.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/src/mobile/android/dev.rs" lines="272-276"}

The feature is documented as "increment on each build", so the behavior may be intended. But a reviewer should confirm whether dev runs should consume version codes at all. If not, skip the increment when `dev` is true.

Before this PR, the build script wrote `tauri.properties` whenever it ran with `TAURI_ANDROID_PROJECT_PATH` set. Now only the CLI writes it. Any Android build that compiles the Rust crate without going through `tauri android build`/`dev` (for example, running `gradlew` or building from Android Studio against an existing project) will use a stale file or the Gradle default of `versionCode=1`, and `versionName` may be missing.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-build/src/lib.rs" lines="499-503"}

I have not verified which entry points set `TAURI_ANDROID_PROJECT_PATH`, so the blast radius is uncertain. The change is still a behavior break and should be called out in the changeset or migration notes, or the generation kept in the build script too.

`generate_tauri_properties` has several branches: auto-increment with and without an existing file, the explicit `version_code`, the semver fallback, the `0` and out-of-range errors, and the dev clamp. None of them is covered by a test in this diff, and the function touches the filesystem, which makes regressions easy to introduce.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/src/mobile/android/mod.rs" lines="625-684"}

A small set of tests against a temp directory would cover the read/increment/write cycle and the error cases. The `0.0.0` ordering regression above would have been caught by one test.

The increment uses `saturating_add(1)`, so overflow is avoided, but nothing checks the upper bound that the explicit `version_code` already validates (`1..=2100000000`). Once the counter reaches the limit, every later build writes a value that Play Store rejects, and the value is written without any warning.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/src/mobile/android/mod.rs" lines="645-645"}

Add a check that bails with a clear message when the incremented value would exceed 2100000000.
